{number: 61}
{title: O That Will Be Glory}
{key: Ab}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[Ab] When all my labors and trials are o'er,
And I am safe on that beautiful [Eb7] shore,
[Ab] Just to be near the dear Lord I adore,
Will thro' the [Eb7] ages be glory for [Ab] me.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
O that will be [Db] glory for [Ab] me,
Glory for [Eb7] me, glory for [Ab] me,
When by His [Ab7] grace I shall [Db] look on His [Bbm] face,
That will be [Ab] glory, be [Eb7] glory for [Ab] me.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[Ab] When by the gift of His infinite grace,
I am accorded in heaven a [Eb7] place,
[Ab] Just to be there and to look on His face,
Will thro' the [Eb7] ages be glory for [Ab] me.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[Ab] Friends will be there I have loved long ago;
Joy like a river around me will [Eb7] flow;
[Ab] Yet just a smile from my Savior, I know,
Will thro' the [Eb7] ages be glory for [Ab] me.
{end_of_verse}
